    {
      "figure_number": 1,
      "label": "fig:algorithm",
      "caption_claim_boundary": "Overview and mechanism detail of the deterministic \\cges{} pipeline. \\textbf{(a)} Complete reports pass candidate and leakage gates; retained sentences receive lexical roles and form a typed textual proxy graph. The normalized $Q$, $R$, $G$, $C$, and $P$ channels feed the same redundancy-aware selector. The registered no-CF ablation sets $C$ to zero without renormalizing the other coefficients. \\textbf{(b)} For candidate node $i$, path-deletion loss is obtained by removing $i$, recomputing qualified-path utility, and taking $C_i=U(G)-U(G\\setminus i)$. The graph is a structural text proxy and does not identify physical causal effects.",
